title: AgarwalUncle_Day1
tags: 
position: -94,-392
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite GeneralStore>>
<<HideCharacter>>

After overhearing his mother discuss struggles of local shopkeepers, Raju visits Agarwal Uncle's general store during busy evening hours to see if he might need assistance.

<<HideCharacter>>

The cramped interior buzzes with evening activity. Customers squeeze between narrow aisles as the shopkeeper moves constantly between tasks.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Tired">>
AgarwalUncle: Arre beta, terrible timing and perfect timing all at once!

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
AgarwalUncle: Half my customers want their monthly supplies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Anxious">>
AgarwalUncle: And the other half need immediate small items.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Pained">>
AgarwalUncle: But I'm just one person trying to serve everyone at once.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: Uncle ji, you look completely overwhelmed!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: The store is so busy today. Is there anything I can do to help you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
AgarwalUncle: Help? Beta, running a general store isn't like playing shop-shop with your friends.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: Real money changes hands here. Customers expect exact change.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
AgarwalUncle: And one mistake in calculations or inventory can cost me profit.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Anxious">>
AgarwalUncle: Profit that feeds my family.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I understand it's serious business, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: But I'm good with numbers and I'm very careful with money.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Maybe I could start with something simple to reduce your workload?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Irritated">>
AgarwalUncle: Simple? Child, there's nothing simple about retail!

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: Every transaction requires checking inventory, calculating totals.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Tired">>
AgarwalUncle: Handling cash, giving correct change.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
AgarwalUncle: And maintaining customer relationships.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Anxious">>
AgarwalUncle: One dissatisfied customer can damage reputation built over twenty years.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to help, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Proud">>
Raju: You've built such a trusted business that serves our entire neighborhood.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Surely there's some way I could assist without causing problems?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Surprised">>
AgarwalUncle: You really want to learn about shopkeeping?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
AgarwalUncle: Even knowing how demanding customers can be?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: How precise money handling must be?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Tired">>
AgarwalUncle: How exhausting these long days become?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I'm not afraid of hard work or demanding customers, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: My father always says that honest business is the backbone of any community.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: And I want to understand what that really means.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Relaxed">>
AgarwalUncle: Your father is a wise man, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
AgarwalUncle: But understanding and doing are very different things.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Then let me learn by doing, uncle. Give me a chance to prove myself.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
AgarwalUncle: Your persistence is admirable, I'll give you that.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Neutral">>
AgarwalUncle: Come back tomorrow morning. We'll talk more when it's not so chaotic.

<<HideCharacter>>

As Raju exits the crowded store, he carries deep appreciation for retail complexity and strengthened determination to prove his commitment.

<<set $AgarwalUncle_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: AgarwalUncle_Day2
tags: 
position: 423,-115
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite GeneralStore>>
<<HideCharacter>>

Despite yesterday's introduction to demanding retail, Raju returns during morning restocking, hoping to observe how Agarwal Uncle prepares for the day.

<<HideCharacter>>

The store emanates methodical efficiency. Agarwal Uncle systematically checks deliveries, updates price lists, and arranges products with precision.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Surprised">>
AgarwalUncle: Back again, beta?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
AgarwalUncle: I thought yesterday's madness might have scared you off.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Relaxed">>
AgarwalUncle: Most people don't see the hours of preparation behind every smooth transaction.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Actually, uncle, watching you yesterday made me more fascinated, not less.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: I've never seen anyone keep track of so many different items.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: So many prices and customer preferences while maintaining perfect accuracy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Amused">>
AgarwalUncle: Perfect accuracy? Ha! Beta, I make mistakes every day.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Embarrassed">>
AgarwalUncle: Miscounting change, ordering wrong quantities, misreading customer needs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Confident">>
AgarwalUncle: The difference is I've learned to catch errors quickly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: And fix them before they become bigger problems.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: How did you develop such detailed knowledge of inventory?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Curious">>
Raju: And customer patterns? Did you study business?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Or learn through experience?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Sad">>
AgarwalUncle: I inherited this store from my father twenty-two years ago.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: When I was barely older than you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Crying">>
AgarwalUncle: He died suddenly, leaving me with suppliers to pay.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
AgarwalUncle: Customers to serve, and a family to support.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Disappointed">>
AgarwalUncle: But no formal business training whatsoever.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: That must have been terrifying, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sympathetic">>
Raju: Taking on such huge responsibility so young, with no preparation or guidance.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: Terrifying, yes. But also necessary.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Proud">>
AgarwalUncle: This store supported my mother, my younger sister's education.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Loving">>
AgarwalUncle: And eventually my own wife and children.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Determined">>
AgarwalUncle: When survival depends on success, you learn faster than any classroom could teach.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: That's incredible, uncle. You built all this expertise through dedication.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Respectful">>
Raju: Through necessity. No wonder you're so careful about every detail.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Understanding">>
Raju: You understand how much depends on getting things right.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Pleased">>
AgarwalUncle: You're beginning to understand, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: Retail isn't just about selling products. It's about serving community.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Proud">>
AgarwalUncle: Building trust. Maintaining relationships that span generations.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Quizzical">>
AgarwalUncle: You keep expressing interest in helping.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
AgarwalUncle: But retail assistance means different responsibilities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
AgarwalUncle: What exactly do you think you could contribute to established business operations?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Thoughtful">>
Raju: I've been thinking about that, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: And I'm ready to show you rather than just tell you.

<<HideCharacter>>

As their conversation concludes with Agarwal Uncle's direct inquiry, Raju recognizes his offers have progressed into serious evaluation.

